From 3398a6b30be44ccb5612ee6d8ea6f7fa7da09976 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Roch=C3=A9=20Compaan?= <roche@upfrontsoftware.co.za>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:20:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/14] qwen35: dense Q6_K weight products on CUDA

Dense qwen35 keeps output.weight and two tensors per layer in Q6_K, so the
CUDA path cannot load the model without it. Decode the 6-bit quant with the
existing value<TYPE> mechanism and register the type in all four dispatch
layers: matvec_dispatch, matrix_dispatch (tensor-core and plain) and the
dense_blas unpack path.

The row stride keeps the n % 256 guard, so K=384 is refused instead of
truncated. The test encodes and decodes Q6_K with its own arithmetic, sweeps
K in {256,512}, M in {1,4} and T in {1,8,9,17,32,33}, repeats 9 and 17 with
the tensor-core layer forced off, and checks the two refusals. A stride of
176 instead of 210 fails the first multi-row case.

Upstream: not offered, fork only
Retire-when: dense qwen35 runs on CUDA upstream
Carried-commits: none (authored here)
